22. PRIVILEGED ACCESS REQUEST

============================================================

IMPORTANT SECURITY RULE:

NEVER ask a user to enter another user's password.

NEVER store another user's password.

NEVER display another user's password.

NEVER implement a workflow that requires sharing credentials.

Instead create a secure conceptual workflow:

User requests privileged access.

→ System identifies protected resource.

→ System identifies responsible authorized user/administrator.

→ Approval request is generated.

→ Authorized user receives notification.

→ Authorized user explicitly approves or rejects.

→ If approved:

Create a temporary, limited-scope access session.

The session must include:

Requester
Approver
Target User/Resource
Reason
Scope
Start Time
Expiration Time
Device
Session ID
Audit Event

The requester must not receive permanent access.

